  "nodes": [
    {
      "id": "b624e13b-e248-5bb7-b66d-8a369a72ff78",
      "name": "Sticky Note",
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.stickyNote",
      "position": [
        -1020,
        -500
      ],
      "parameters": {
        "width": 600,
        "height": 880,
        "content": "## Screen Google Sheets leads for cold email compliance\n\nChecks every new lead in your sheet with [Precleared](https://precleared.dev) and writes the answer next to it, so you know who you can cold email before anyone writes a word. Covers UK PECR and GDPR, US CAN-SPAM, Canada's CASL, Germany's UWG and French rules.\n\n### Who's it for\nAnyone who keeps prospects in Google Sheets and sends cold email, by hand or from another workflow.\n\n### How it works\n1. **Every morning** reads your sheet and keeps the rows that have no verdict yet.\n2. **Check with Precleared** asks whether a cold email to each address is allowed.\n3. **Write the verdict back** fills in the verdict, the rule behind it, the next step, what the email's footer must include and a signed receipt id.\n\nA row Precleared couldn't answer (for example, once the day's free checks are used) stays blank, with the reason in `note`, and is tried again on the next run.\n\n### How to set up\n1. Make a sheet with these column headers: `email`, `address_source`, `verdict`, `rule`, `next_step`, `footer_requirement`, `receipt_id`, `checked_at`, `note`. In `address_source`, say where each address came from: published, bought, scraped, given or unknown (blank counts as unknown).\n2. Pick that sheet in **Read leads** and in **Write the verdict back**.\n3. Fill in **Your settings**: your country (GB or US) and what you offer.\n4. Run it once to check, then switch it on so it runs every morning.\n\n### Requirements\n- A Google account for Sheets.\n- No Precleared account: 10 free checks a day, shared by everyone on your IP address. A free key from [precleared.dev/get-key](https://precleared.dev/get-key) gives you your own 25 a day (best on n8n Cloud). To use it, set **Check with Precleared** to Header Auth with the name `Authorization` and the value `Bearer pc_live_...`.\n\n### How to customize\n- Change the schedule, or run it when a row is added.\n- Raise `max_checks_per_run` once you have a key or a pack.\n- Send the `ok_to_email` rows on to your email workflow.\n\nPrecleared is decision support with sources, not legal advice."
      },
      "typeVersion": 1
    },
